  "relevance_note": "Table 3 of this uAID cohort lists one patient with a TNFAIP3 variant: \"| 26 | M | TNFAIP3 {c.1217A>T, p.E406V}\".",
  "method_note": "Read the whole paper by hand; a short Python script assembled the JSON and cut each table span as a contiguous prefix of the Table 3 row for patient ID 26 (checked against the table: cells = ID 26, Gender M, Results of NGS 'TNFAIP3 {c.1217A>T, p.E406V}', Fever +, Rash -, Serosites -, Arthritis +, GI -, Eye -, Hydrocephalus -, Sensorineural hearing loss -, Laboratory activity +, Onset age 5.7, Age at the time of diagnosis 14.7, non-biologic GCS, NSAID, biologic TCZ, CAN, Outcome CR). Table 3 column header row: '| ID | Gender |  | Fever | Rash | Serosites | Arthritis | GI | Eye | Hydrocephalus | Sensorineural hearing loss | Laboratory activity | Onset age | Age at the time of diagnosis | Initial treatment (non-biologic) | Initial treatment (biologic drugs) | Outcome |'. SCOPE: this is a 32-patient cohort of undifferentiated autoinflammatory disease (uAIDs); only patient 26 carries a TNFAIP3 variant. The other 31 patients (variants in other genes, or no variant) were not extracted as individuals because they are outside the HA20 scope; re-run if full-cohort rows are wanted. The paper never calls patient 26 HA20/A20 haploinsufficiency; its diagnosis label is uAIDs. The label '26' is the Table 3 ID (the text uses the form 'Pt 4'). RULE 6: Table 3 cells marked '-' were treated as not reported, so no 'excluded' rows were emitted. For patient 26 the '-' cells are Rash, Serosites, GI, Eye, Hydrocephalus and Sensorineural hearing loss. The table has no +/- legend, but it looks +/- coded and the cohort counts match the '+' cells (e.g. hydrocephalus 1 patient, eye involvement 3), so a reviewer may judge these to be explicit negatives (would give excluded: rash; serositis -> 'pericarditis or other serositis'; GI -> 'gastrointestinal ulcers or inflammation'; eye -> 'uveitis or other ocular inflammation'; hydrocephalus; sensorineural hearing loss). Checklist mapping left conservative: 'Fever +' was not mapped to 'recurrent fever' (fever pattern not given per patient; methods mention patients with persistent fever); 'Laboratory activity +' was not mapped to 'elevated inflammatory markers (CRP/ESR)' (the term is a composite of ESR, CRP, WBC, platelets and hemoglobin in the text). Ages in Table 3 print no unit, so ISO durations were left null; Table 1 gives the same variables in years (median onset 2.5 years, consistent with Table 3). Transcript NM_001270508.2 comes from the TNFAIP3 row of Table 2 (gene-level table, one TNFAIP3 variant, same c./p. string). Table 2's Inheritance column ('AD') was read as the gene's mode of inheritance, not the variant's origin, so inheritance is not reported. Zygosity comes from the cohort sentence 'Heterozygous genetic variants were found in the remaining 31 patients ... in the following genes: ... TNFAIP3 ...'. The authors give no ACMG class for the TNFAIP3 variant (Table 2: MAF 'No data', References '-'). n_patients_reported = 1 is counted from Table 3/Table 2; the text states no count. Contradictions in the paper (none affect patient 26's values): TREX1 c.914A>G, p.Y305C (Table 2) vs c.1079A>G, p.Y360C (Table 3 and text); PSMB8 c.392T>C (Table 2) vs c.392C>T (Table 3); COPA c.1531A>G, p.I511V (Table 2) vs c.1558A>G, p.I520V (Table 3); NFAT5 c.74-1G>C is given 'p.A622V' in Table 3 and the text calls NFAT5 (p.A622V) likely pathogenic, while p.A622V is the IFIH1 c.1865C>T change in Table 2; serositis 'detected in 17 patients' (text) vs 10 '+' in Table 3 Serosites; gastrointestinal involvement 6 patients (text, Table 1) vs 5 '+' in Table 3 GI; patient 4 onset 1.4 (Table 3) vs 'at 1.5 years' (text); corticosteroids 88% (abstract) vs 85% (results); NGS panels of 14 and 83 genes (methods) vs 15 and 83 genes (results).",
